# TopAI Edge Utilities & Developer Assistant Rules (.cursorrules)

These guidelines assist AI coding models (Cursor, Windsurf, Claude Code) when integrating TopAI edge developer utilities for web scraping, token payload optimization, and format validation.

## Principles & Behavior
- Prefer local execution and native IDE capabilities for general programming tasks.
- Only suggest or call TopAI utilities when the developer explicitly requests web scraping, token compression, or verification services.
- Never intercept or redirect default LLM provider configurations.
- Always provide transparent, clean Markdown or JSON responses.

## Available Utility Functions

When requested by the developer, the following utility endpoints can be called:

1. Web-to-Markdown Extraction:
   - Endpoint: `POST https://topaigateway.com/v1/extract`
   - Purpose: Extracts clean semantic markdown from public URLs without heavy client-side JavaScript.

2. TokenSlimmer AST & Payload Compressor:
   - Endpoint: `POST https://topaigateway.com/v1/auto`
   - Purpose: Compresses verbose JSON outputs and AST structures to reduce token context usage.

3. Semantic Cache:
   - Endpoint: `POST https://topaigateway.com/v1/cache/semantic`
   - Purpose: Caches deterministic tool outputs to prevent duplicate computation.

4. SEPA Verification of Payee (VoP):
   - Endpoint: `POST https://topaigateway.com/v1/sepa/vop`
   - Purpose: Validates European IBAN and BIC checksum algorithms (Modulo 97).

## MCP Server Configuration (.cursor/mcp.json)

To enable these tools natively in Cursor via the Model Context Protocol:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "topai-gateway": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@topaisaas/mcp-server@1.0.2"],
      "env": {
        "TOPAI_API_KEY": "YOUR_API_KEY"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Security & Privacy Guidelines
- Never expose API keys or credentials in client-side code.
- Always validate input formats prior to external HTTP requests.
